<title>UK: Bank of Beirut sets $50 million three-year bond.</title>
<headline>Bank of Beirut sets $50 million three-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Paribas and Middle East Capital Group.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANK OF BEIRUT</p>
<p> AMT     $50 MLN	COUPON     8.875     MATURITY    05.JUN.00</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.884    PAY DATE    05.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.0	 REOFFER    99.884    SPREAD	+250 BP</p>
<p> DENOMS (K) 50	  LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.75	SELL CONC  0.25	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 3-YEAR U.S. TREASURY</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
